The change links shared AGENTS.md into Delta's personal rules directory.
Delta discovers personal skills directly under ~/.agents/skills, so it needs
no extra skill links. The directory choices and AGENT.md precedence follow:
https://delta.dev/docs/configuration/settings#rules
https://delta.dev/docs/agents/skills

Validation on Linux in an isolated /tmp clone:
- sh -n install: exit 0.
- git diff --check: exit 0.
- Python 3 ran the actual installer via subprocess.run(['sh', installer]),
  copying install, AGENTS.md, and lore into each temporary
  HOME/.agents/skills directory. HOME was overridden only in child-process
  environments; the real home and installed checkout were untouched.
- Each fixture had a directory name containing spaces. XDG_CONFIG_HOME and
  DELTA_CONFIG_DIR were removed from inherited test environments unless the
  case set them. A PATH-prefixed uname stub selected Linux or Darwin.
- Five successful fixtures, each rerun to check idempotence: Linux defaults;
  Linux with XDG_CONFIG_HOME; Linux with DELTA_CONFIG_DIR and XDG_CONFIG_HOME;
  Darwin with XDG_CONFIG_HOME (must be ignored); Darwin with DELTA_CONFIG_DIR.
  Assertions checked AGENTS.md was a symlink to this checkout's AGENTS.md,
  the existing Claude lore link still resolved correctly, and each second
  run exited 0 with no output.
- Three occupied-destination fixtures: regular file, symlink to an existing
  different file, dangling symlink. Every run exited 1 with "is in the way"
  and preserved the destination's original contents or symlink target.

Result: all 8 fixtures passed (13 installer invocations total).
This verifies path selection and installer behavior, not Delta's runtime
rules reload. Darwin was simulated for path selection, not run on macOS.
